Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:37:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(telegram): pure rules for copy-command buttons

Derives copyable shell commands from an already-generated reply by fixed
rules, so the behaviour does not depend on the model choosing to emit a
button. The core is pure (str -> commands) and imports only stdlib; the
two PTB-facing helpers degrade to no button when CopyTextButton is absent.

Only bash/sh/shell fences qualify. A fence is one unit, so it yields one
button carrying every line. Blocks that look like output (timestamps, log
levels, tracebacks, ls listings) are skipped, and a block over Telegram's
256-character copy_text limit gets no button rather than being truncated.

